    "background_story": "Zayla was a renowned food critic known for her scathing reviews of the city's top restaurants. Her colleagues described her as stodgy, with an unyielding commitment to traditional cuisine and a disdain for innovation. Zayla's palate was refined, but her expectations were impossibly high. She would often send dishes back to the kitchen, deeming them unworthy of her attention. Despite her tough exterior, Zayla had a soft spot for family-owned eateries and hidden gems. She would go to great lengths to support these underdog establishments, using her influence to bring them to the forefront of the culinary scene. Zayla's stodgy demeanor belied a deep passion for good food and a desire to preserve the art of traditional cooking.",
